#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: ascii -*-
"""
patch_ask_prof_2026_10_23.py  ASK_PROF_2026_10_23

The Professor (BRAIN_PATH B4; RELATIONS_AND_ASK A1, ask-v2), on the PC's Ask page.

  scripts/dashboard.py  /api/ask takes "mode": "professor" (else the verses, as before). Then the model is given the
                        scholarly English where a verse has it (else the working English) and the IAST; the names the
                        verses name and whom our texts name them with (entity_links); what Raychaudhuri's Political
                        History says of those names (data/shelf/claims.db, the latest read of each page); the relations
                        the indexes state of them, already checked (data/shelf/kin.db: words in the entry, direction
                        agreeing). Each statement of a scholar or an index is numbered [S1] ... and cited so. The
                        instruction: only the evidence given; keep apart what the verses say, what the scholars state
                        and what is inferred, and how firm; never a scholar from memory; never as any real person. All
                        read-only and free but the answer, metered as "ask_prof" (about $0.003 a question with Flash).
                        The answer's JSON adds ask_mode and scholarly (names, items, what was read).
  scripts/ask.html      Verses | Professor (remembered in this browser); the [S] statements as violet citations, and
                        under the answer "The scholars and the indexes" with the names and whom they are named with;
                        "What this answer read" says what the Professor was given.

The page shows at once; the Professor answers after the dashboard is restarted (when it is idle). Needs
ASK_UI_2026_10_22 in both files. Marker-idempotent per file, all-or-nothing, backup first (.bak_askprof_<date>), line
endings kept, py_compile before anything is written.

  python scripts\\patch_ask_prof_2026_10_23.py --check
  python scripts\\patch_ask_prof_2026_10_23.py
"""
